SOURCE CODE FOR NETWORK USERS (SECTION 13)
==========================================

When this program runs in HTTP mode, people can interact with it over a
network.  The program offers them its Corresponding Source through the
"journal_about" MCP tool, the "kairos-journal://about" MCP resource, the
GET /about HTTP endpoint and the server's MCP instructions.  Each of these
reports the source location configured in the KAIROS_JOURNAL_SOURCE_URL
environment variable or, by default, in the "kairosJournal.sourceUrl" field
of package.json.  If you modify this program and let others use it over a
network, set that location to where your modified source can be downloaded
at no charge.


